flowchart LR
  subgraph env["One uv-managed venv — one Python, ordinary Python package deps only;\nthe same on both floors: Linux + NVIDIA and Apple Silicon"]
    app["Stream\n(stream.py: @stream functions over a StreamBuilder compile the stream's graph\nfrom @node.process classes, ports declared as Input / Output class attributes — hosts no node;\ndecided, unbuilt: GraphInput and GraphOutput nodes declare a graph's interface at every level —\nno expose — Get/SetVariable nodes carry a value or a node reference with no wire,\nand add takes a @stream as a subgraph;\ncompiled in the project's own interpreter;\nthe graph is data — one shape with what the runtime renders live — that a runtime runs)"]
    procs["Node classes\n(importable modules — imported by the stream,\ndescribed in the stream's own interpreter when a graph naming them loads, run by processor interpreters;\nnever hosted in the stream's process or the runtime process;\nthe class's import path is its identity)"]
    pkgs["Extension wheels\n(ordinary PyPI packages — Rust inside for speed, a Python node\nas the binding; depend on tatolab-stream, never on the runtime, never link the engine;\nnative internals expose handles, never streamlib internals;\none mechanism — a processor extension added by stream_builder.add that calls its own\nRust directly; no package extends the engine, each sets itself up where its nodes run,\nand an engine-grade capability enters as a built-in; first-party optional capabilities ship this way too,\nnetworking shipped first — tatolab-webrtc (tatolab.webrtc: WhipPublisher / WhepPlayer), on the encoded\nside of the codec blocks, touching no surface and no GPU;\nlive in packages/, local-linked in-repo, published to PyPI beside tatolab-stream)"]
    wheel["tatolab-stream and the lend\n(tatolab-stream (tatolab.stream): pure Python from PyPI, every stream venv installs it,\nand a stream imports, type-checks, compiles and is tested with no runtime present;\nbuilt-in nodes are classes generated from the runtime's descriptors with typed configs;\nwhat the runtime backs is declared once there as Protocols and runtime-backed functions,\nheld to both binaries by a conformance gate, so the two floors are one surface and an\nabsent capability is a closed list refused by name; no public Python name says processor;\ntatolab.runtime: the native bindings and the processor-interpreter bootstrap, built into\nthe runtime unit's lend directory beside tatolabd and tatolab — never on pip, never in a\nvenv; it carries the Vulkan loader and the driver a stock machine lacks, named to the loader additively —\nMoltenVK on macOS, and on Linux the software device, headless lavapipe, taken last;\none version number for everything released from this repository — tatolab-stream,\nthe runtime and the first-party extensions, released together;\nports are Input / Output class attributes of one of five families, so pyright types each read)"]
    helper["Processor interpreters — every Python node\n(engine exec of the stream's own venv interpreter, with the\nruntime's lend directory (holding tatolab/runtime/) prepended to PYTHONPATH;\nown interpreter, own GIL; imports the lent tatolab.runtime, not a wheel in\nits venv, beside the venv's tatolab.stream;\nrefuses to start unless that runtime is the\nparent's own engine build, id checked before\nany channel or socket opens;\nthe only placement)"]
  end

  rustapp["Rust app\n(plain cargo project)"]
  crate["streamlib crate\n(embeddable Rust library)"]
  engine["Engine runtime\n(runtime/streamlib-engine, hosted by the native tatolabd — no Python in its process;\none runtime per machine runs many streams: tatolabd takes no stream, never detaches,\nand holds the machine lock — owned by one user, another user's runtime refused by name;\non macOS the lock is the loopback HTTP port 127.0.0.1:4446 tatolabd binds itself, no root,\nits holder named by the pid it answers;\none Runner — one GpuContext, iceoryx2 node, tokio runtime, surface service and local API —\nand a table of loaded streams, each with its own graph, event topic, Python node types,\nshutdown, watchdog and its own stream clock, real, scaled or stepped; no link crosses a stream's edge — a stream reads\nanother's track only through gateway nodes (decided, unbuilt);\nevery loaded stream recorded in the state directory under its stream id — computed from its\nlocation, the project directory and stream function — and re-loaded at every start unless\nstopped or failed, a stream\nin the runtime's last two crashes in a row recorded failed;\neach project's .venv made with the uv the runtime unit carries whenever its interpreter\ndoes not run, and a stream whose venv or code fails recorded failed, never refused;\ndecided, unbuilt: tatolabd holds no publisher, no relay adapter and no relay — nothing leaves a stream on its own;\nstarted by Tato Studio as its child while the app runs, from the runtime unit its bundle carries,\nor in a terminal over the build curl | sh installed; no installer registers a service)"]
  media["Media modules and engine media primitives\n(the runtime ships no media nodes and opens no windows;\ncamera, microphone, speaker, H.264 / H.265, Opus, TestPatternSource and the Linux-only\nVirtualCameraSink are modules — tatolab-camera, tatolab-microphone, tatolab-speaker,\ntatolab-h264, tatolab-h265, tatolab-opus, tatolab-testpattern, tatolab-virtualcamera —\neach a node in its own helper process, typed by its own import path (tatolab.camera:CameraSource),\nits native half reaching ports through the module host table;\nthe engine keeps the primitives they use: capture on one video device seam — V4L2 on Linux,\nAVFoundation on Apple — the audio backend per platform, colour conversion behind\nconvert_surface_into, surface import by plane layout;\nvideo codecs run on a device the module owns — streamlib-vulkan-video on Linux, VideoToolbox on Apple;\nthe virtual camera is one camera per node, created at setup and removed at teardown —\na v4l2loopback device through the module's control node, the loopback permission a one-time\nenable-virtual-camera, or a PipeWire camera node the module opens through the host table;\ndecided, unbuilt: RelayTrackSource leaves the runtime as tatolab.moq:MoqTrackReceive; a former built-in's type is refused at load\nnaming the module to install)"]
  rhi["RHI\n(accelerators optional — the engine never runs without a device: the first stream to start\nbuilds the one GpuContext on the first device the engine can build on, hardware before the\nbundled software device, and every tier that device lacks refuses by name at the node;\nvulkan/rhi + streamlib-consumer-rhi —\nthe one Vulkan RHI on both floors, MoltenVK the macOS driver;\nMetal only as handles exported from Vulkan objects;\na driver's missing capability is an absent tier refused by name;\nframe count is per node, memory per runtime — every frame allocation\nrefused by name past the device's memory budget; the shared pools cap\nno shape, never wait, and give memory back at stream stop and when idle)"]
  interop["Interop adapters\n(app-process Rust, per floor — Vulkan, cpu-readback, skia on both;\nVulkan↔GL and Vulkan↔CUDA on Linux, named absent on macOS)"]
  ctl["Control plane — the local API\n(api-server: HTTP / WS / MCP — hosted by the engine;\nserved on local-api.sock in the runtime directory, which only the owning user can open —\none socket per machine, no network address serves control, and another machine's streams\nare changed on that machine (ssh) or by the control client;\nMCP through rmcp: POST /mcp at its latest revision alone (2026-07-28), and /mcp/stdio\nat every revision it speaks, preferring the latest, for MCP hosts,\nwhich launch the CLI's mcp verb, a byte pipe to the socket (ssh for another machine); closing a connection unloads no stream;\nserves the node catalog — every registered type with its derived\nconfig schema and ports — the live graph, and recipes over its tools, all in the\ngraph's words — add_node / remove_node, connect by node name and port, every tool naming its\nstream; the stream actions run_project / stop_stream / start_stream / remove_project /\nrename_stream / list_streams / describe_stream_action / cancel_stream_action —\nevery load and unload queued as a stream action and answered at once with its action id,\none serial queue per project; rename sets a record attribute at once;\nrun_project takes a project directory and loads every stream in it, every action on an\nexisting stream names it by its stream id; logs takes the project; no shutdown verb;\nthe listing and the lock holder's pid on loopback — no snapshot form, no HTTP off loopback,\nno tailscale serve; decided, unbuilt: no relay verbs — a gateway's URL and credential are its node config, or a Records message on its settings input from a node reading a secret store;\ndecided, unbuilt: a viewer's read of any port by family for Tato Studio)"]
  cli["CLI — the native tatolab beside tatolabd, never on pip, linking no engine\nnew · run / dev / stop / start / rm / cancel / streams · graph / logs · mcp · enable-virtual-camera\n(every stream verb a call into the one running runtime, which compiles the stream in the\nproject's venv interpreter; a load or unload verb exits once its stream action is queued,\nand logs / dev read the project's one log; with no runtime each fails at the socket and starts none;\nshipped with the runtime by the installer; new scaffolds the sample stream —\nTestPatternSource → HalftoneLensEffect (a Slang compute kernel), seen in a viewer — plus a numpy meter,\nand never a camera; the cross-floor check's warnings reach the project's log and never block a start)"]
  wire["Wire\n(messages between nodes — an engine-owned envelope carrying the starts_group flag, a payload\ndescriptor of the port's family and a payload; five families — Image, Array, Channels, Packets,\nRecords — compared at connect, each with its own descriptor, a Records dict encoded by the runtime\nand msgpack out of user code; a by-name write's bytes pass through as written;\nthe encoding named in the writer's catalog entry, a hang entry; a read tells what its link lost since the last one (lost_since_last_read)\n— the only cross-language boundary;\na fixed descriptor in the iceoryx2 user header, reads borrowed in place, writes loaned,\na per-link borrow quota, GPU pool slots imported once and claimed in a shared-memory claim table)"]

  registry["Runtime and state directories\n(the one engine-resolved runtime directory — on Linux XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/streamlib where that\nis set and non-empty, otherwise, and on macOS always, /tmp/streamlib-<uid>, owner-only and\nchecked before the first write — holds the local API socket, the surface socket and the\nengine-owned iceoryx2 domain; the state directory — XDG_STATE_HOME/tatolab, or\n~/Library/Application Support/Tatolab — holds each stream's record and the runtime's own log)"]
  sharing["Sharing — gateway nodes in the tatolab-moq module (decided, unbuilt):\nTatolab is a simple SDK for defining live streams as pipes and sharing them with people and agents;\nthe runtime reads, configures and requires nothing of Tailscale; robotics is out of scope;\ninside a stream nodes share data through shared memory; nothing leaves a stream on its own —\nno publisher, no exposure, no routing policy, no relay run by the runtime;\na gateway node holds one connection to a relay, its URL and credential in its own config,\nand publishes one broadcast <root>/<broadcast>.hang; a track node declares one track on it with its catalog entry\nand is held as a graph variable; a track send node names its track by node reference — a reference edge, never a link —\nand forwards payload bytes as written, groups from starts_group, whole groups dropped under backpressure;\na track receive node reads a remote track, the one way a graph reads a relay, through the one relay-track reader\nit shares with tatolab-read-track — groups released in sequence order, a missing group given up only on its reset,\nthe track's end or newer content past max_age in the track's own time, a give-up reaching readers as lost_since_last_read;\none gateway implementation per relay kind — moq-relay, Cloudflare, moq.pro — carrying dialect, credential, root and catalog cadence;\npreviews come straight from the runtime — Tato Studio's viewers per family, no relay;\nverification is a tool outside the runtime reading a relay the rig starts; the runtime opens no windows;\non the moq-dev line (moq-net, moq-tokio, hang) at exact pins, in the module"]

  ctlclient["External control client\n(decided, not yet built: an extension point —\nstreamlib runs complete without one; how it plugs in is OPEN;\nwhat it hands the runtime is open — gateways carry their own relay settings)"]
